    "section": "Ordering Schematic for Mark 96AA"
  },
  "note": "Extracted by hand from the two page ordering schematic, the 95AA pattern on the reducing side with the gauge port back in the head, left blank when not needed. The inch size brackets on the body Cv, trim, o-ring, range and PED sections are enforced, with the DN twins matched as an inferred coupling; the DN15 rows sit outside every inch bracket, there being no half inch row on this sheet, so they are left unconstrained and held for John. The starred 3-8 range must use the EPDM or ultra-thin Jorlon diaphragm. The body Cv letter is matched to the trim Cv rows as an inferred coupling. Retrofit kits are order notes, not positions.",
